{"title":"Longest Common Substring","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given two strings `s` and `t` made of lowercase English letters. Find the **longest substring that appears in both** of them. A substring is a block of consecutive characters, unlike a subsequence.\n\nPrint the substring itself, not just its length. If several common substrings share the maximum length, print the one that starts **earliest in `s`**. If the two strings have no character in common, print `-1`.\n\nThe interviewer's hint was a 2D DP table in which each cell stores the length of the common substring ending at that pair of positions, together with the index where the best length was reached so the answer can be rebuilt.","inputFormat":"The first line contains the string `s`.\nThe second line contains the string `t`.","outputFormat":"Print the longest common substring (earliest start in `s` on ties), or `-1` if there is none.","constraints":["1 ≤ |s|, |t| ≤ 1500","s and t consist of lowercase English letters"],"examples":[{"input":"xabcdyz\nqabcdzabc","output":"abcd","explanation":"`abcd` appears in both strings and has length 4. The only other common pieces, such as `abc` or `z`, are shorter."},{"input":"abxcd\ncdab","output":"ab","explanation":"`ab` and `cd` are both common substrings of length 2. `ab` starts at index 0 in `s` while `cd` starts at index 3, so `ab` is printed."},{"input":"abc\ndef","output":"-1","explanation":"The strings share no letter, so there is no common substring."}],"tests":[{"input":"a\na","output":"a"},{"input":"a\nb","output":"-1"},{"input":"aaaa\naa","output":"aa"},{"input":"abcabc\nabcabc","output":"abcabc"},{"input":"abcde\nfabcdg","output":"abcd"},{"input":"zzzz\nyyyyz","output":"z"},{"input":"ababab\nbababa","output":"ababa"},{"input":"bba\nabaaabaa","output":"ba"},{"input":"aba\naaaa","output":"a"},{"input":"aac\nbbbac","output":"ac"},{"input":"bcc\nba","output":"b"},{"input":"cws\nq","output":"-1"},{"input":"gog\nkfjstecb","output":"-1"},{"input":"baaab\nabba","output":"ba"},{"input":"abbaa\nbbbbb","output":"bb"},{"input":"baaaa\naacccccab","output":"aa"},{"input":"aaacc\nbcb","output":"c"},{"input":"sfjaw\niivovo","output":"-1"},{"g":52,"n":3001,"ih":"1377b75aa70349f83a8d01ffbaef8110c73e36f53e9a16fc11560bbdc5d3c437","oh":"b935f6b7a9c56a15e7b99c8d6d4b5e918f5a68fafc4490544a446b2ae47bf809"},{"input":"\","output":"bababaabbaaabbabbabb"},{"input":"\","output":""},{"input":"\","output":""}],"complexity":{"time":"O(|s| · |t|)","space":"O(|t|)"},"hints":["Let L[i][j] be the length of the longest common substring that ends exactly at s[i] and t[j]. What is it when s[i] != t[j]?","When s[i] == t[j], L[i][j] = L[i-1][j-1] + 1; otherwise it is 0. The answer is the largest value anywhere in the table.","Remember where the maximum was reached (the end index in s) so you can cut out the substring. Only the previous row is needed, and updating only on a strictly larger length gives the earliest start in s."],"starters":{"python":"import sys\n\n\ndef longest_common_substring(s: str, t: str) -> str:\n    # Write your solution here\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    res = longest_common_substring(data[0], data[1])\n    print(res if res else -1)\n\n\nmain()\n","javascript":"function longestCommonSubstring(s, t) {\n  // Write your solution here\n  return \"\"\n}\n\nconst parts = input.split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean)\nconst res = longestCommonSubstring(parts[0], parts[1])\nconsole.log(res.length > 0 ? res : \"-1\")\n","cpp":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstring longestCommonSubstring(const string& s, const string& t) {\n    // Write your solution here\n    return \"\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    string s, t;\n    cin >> s >> t;\n    string res = longestCommonSubstring(s, t);\n    if (res.empty()) cout << -1 << \"\\n\";\n    else cout << res << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static String longestCommonSubstring(String s, String t) {\n        // Write your solution here\n        return \"\";\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        String s = st.nextToken();\n        String t = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine()).nextToken();\n        String res = longestCommonSubstring(s, t);\n        System.out.println(res.isEmpty() ? \"-1\" : res);\n    }\n}\n"},"reconstructed":true,"generator":"def gen(rng):\n    def word(n, alpha):\n        return \"\".join(rng.choice(alpha) for _ in range(n))\n\n    tests = [\n        \"xabcdyz\\nqabcdzabc\",\n        \"abc\\ndef\",\n        \"abxcd\\ncdab\",\n        \"a\\na\",\n        \"a\\nb\",\n        \"aaaa\\naa\",\n        \"abcabc\\nabcabc\",\n        \"abcde\\nfabcdg\",\n        \"zzzz\\nyyyyz\",\n        \"ababab\\nbababa\",\n    ]\n    for n in (3, 5, 8, 12, 20, 30):\n        for alpha in (\"ab\", \"abc\", \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"):\n            for _ in range(2):\n                tests.append(word(n, alpha) + \"\\n\" + word(rng.randint(1, n + 5), alpha))\n    # plant a long shared piece\n    for _ in range(4):\n        core = word(rng.randint(5, 25), \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\")\n        a = word(rng.randint(0, 20), \"abc\") + core + word(rng.randint(0, 20), \"abc\")\n        b = word(rng.randint(0, 20), \"abc\") + core + word(rng.randint(0, 20), \"abc\")\n        tests.append(a + \"\\n\" + b)\n    # mid-size\n    tests.append(word(500, \"ab\") + \"\\n\" + word(700, \"ab\"))\n    tests.append(word(800, \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\") + \"\\n\" + word(800, \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"))\n    # max-size cases\n    N = 1500\n    tests.append(\"a\" * N + \"\\n\" + \"a\" * N)\n    tests.append(word(N, \"ab\") + \"\\n\" + word(N, \"ab\"))\n    core = word(600, \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\")\n    tests.append(word(450, \"abc\") + core + word(450, \"abc\") + \"\\n\" + word(300, \"abc\") + core + word(600, \"abc\"))\n    half = \"a\" * 700\n    tests.append(half + \"b\" + half + \"\\n\" + half + \"c\" + half)\n    return tests\n","seed":20261020}